    fix(snagging): Copy as new: the backend writes both aggregates in one idempotent call
    
    Copying a notification created only the canonical notification-fulfilments
    document, never the paired Notification at the copy's new reference, so the
    copy was missing from the dashboard and the first save, submit, amend or
    delete 404'd onto the recoverable-error page.
    
    NotificationFulfilmentsService.copy now calls
    NotificationService.createCopyAtReference inside its existing transaction,
    writing the paired Notification at the copy's reference and only on the
    non-dedupe path, so an idempotent replay still yields exactly one of each.
    The copied Notification carries the source's content verbatim, and a
    fulfilments document with no paired Notification still yields an empty DRAFT
    so the copy stays listable and self-heals on first save.
    
    The half-writing POST /notifications/{ref}/copy endpoint,
    NotificationService.copyNotification and NotificationCopyMapper are deleted
    along with their tests; the tests repo's unused notification API client
    copyNotification goes with them and gains getNotification.
    
    E2E specs now assert both aggregates: the dashboard shows the copy as a Draft
    card mirroring the source, a copy can be edited, saved and submitted
    end-to-end, and the promoted-lifecycle spec checks the notification side of
    copy and its replay. The frontend keeps its single Idempotency-Key call;
    only persistence.md changes, to record copy as the exception to the
    canonical-then-projection write order.
    
    Increment: snag-001 (EUDPA-317, parent EUDPA-315)
    
